            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0042-118461</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With a rate of less than 2 %, retreatment after SMILE is rare. If a touch-up is required, there are different options to choose from: surface ablation (PRK/LASEK) with Mitomycin C, the standard femto-flap procedure with the same parameters, the CIRCLE procedure, which extends the previous SMILE interface into a flap, or the innovative but off-label capless SMILE procedure, which preserves all the advantages of SMILE.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Georg Thieme Verlag KG Stuttgart · New York.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
